WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.480
The Invisible Reality: The Wonderful Weirdness of the Quantum World

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.500
Good evening.

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:10.580
Thank you.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.980
About a hundred years ago,

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.860
a single generation of physicists...

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:25.220
their work caused a radical upheaval in our understanding of the natural world,

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:28.200
our understanding of reality.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:31.900
And its kind of surprising that, you know, 100 years later,

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.900
These insights have not been

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.900
widely absorbed

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:38.080
by the general public, but

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:40.340
what is the case is that our

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.340
culture has certainly

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:44.340
adopted the language of quantum

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:46.340
mechanics, because for instance,

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.340
If we take a look at things

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:50.340
like the quantum

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.340
sleeper.

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:54.340
Every loving couple

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:56.340
should have one of these.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.340
It gives protection from biochemical

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:00.340
terrorist attacks,

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:02.340
protection from natural disasters, from kid knappers

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:04.340
stalkers. It's a bullet proof

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:06.340
safe room; and you just have to

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:08.340
sleep inside, sort of like...like...

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:10.340
like dracula. Umm...

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:12.340
What I'd like to

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.340
do here tonight, though, is

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.340
just go a little bit

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:16.900
further

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:18.340
than the language.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:20.340
of quantum physics

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:22.340
and try to give you a sense

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:24.340
of the logical progression

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:25.360
of ideas

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:26.220
that led

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:28.340
to this new picture of reality that you saw a little bit

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:30.340
about in the previous video sequence

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:32.340
and then we'll take

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:34.340
up some of the ideas

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:36.340
that physicists are still struggling with

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:38.340
today. So, what I'd like

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:40.340
to do toward that end

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:42.340
is, basically look

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:44.340
at a sequence

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:46.340
of experiments - each one of which

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:48.340
is pretty simple

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:50.340
to describe. Pretty simple

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:52.340
to explain.

